            <div xml:id="d183">

                <pb facs="0563" n="518" xml:id="pg518"/>

                <head>183. Memorandum From Director of Central Intelligence Turner to the Deputy Director of Central
                    Intelligence (Carlucci), the Deputy
                    Director for Operations (McMahon), and
                    the National Intelligence Officer for China ([<hi rendition="#italic">name not
                        declassified</hi>])<anchor n="1" xml:id="d183-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1980-01-29">January 29, 1980</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <list subtype="subject" type="description">
                    <label>SUBJECT</label>
                    <item>Conversation with Secretary and Deputy Secretary of Defense, 28 January
                        1980 (U)</item>
                </list>
                <p>1. We talked about the Secretary’s trip to China with regard to [<hi
                        rendition="#italic">less than 1 line not declassified</hi>]
                        Afghanistan.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d183-f2"/> [<hi rendition="#italic">8
                        lines and 1 paragraph (6 lines) not declassified</hi>]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#bold">Stansfield
                                Turner</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
